   "translation": {
    "literal": "With body, speech, mind or senses, with intellect or self, or from the disposition of nature — whatever I do, all of it I offer to the Supreme, thinking “to Nārāyaṇa”.",
    "readable": "Whatever I do — with body, speech or mind, with the senses, the intellect or the self, or simply because my nature leads me to it — I offer all of it to the Supreme, to Nārāyaṇa."
   }
  }
 ],
 "meaning": "The rite ends by giving itself away. Every agency by which anything is done is named — body, speech, mind, the senses, intellect, the self, and finally the inborn tendencies of one’s nature — and whatever has been done through any of them, the rite just completed included, is offered to the Supreme, Nārāyaṇa. M follows it with ॐ तत्सत् ब्रह्मार्पणमस्तु (tat-sat).",
 "in_the_rite": "Step samarpaṇa, all three services, the last verse of the rite before ācamana.",
 "notes": [
  {
   "label": "linguistic",
   "text": "Upajāti metre (mixed indravajrā and upendravajrā): four pādas of eleven syllables. S writes बुद्‌ध्याऽऽत्मना with a double avagraha, marking the ā of ātmanā; M writes बुद्ध्याऽत्मना."
  }
 ],
